# Build-context excludes for Containerfile.bakeoff (kube/benchmark-runner-
# job.yaml's power-agent-bench-lite:local image). `podman build` otherwise
# sends the *entire* local checkout as build context regardless of
# .gitignore (that file only governs git, not container build context), so
# without this file a `COPY . .` step would ship this repo's 1.3G .venv/
# and 187M logs/ into the image and/or fail on files that don't belong
# there.
#
# data/*.m (the CSIRO case files `scripts/fetch_csiro_nem_data.py` fetches)
# is deliberately *not* excluded here: orchestrator.py's --step sweep needs
# data/snem1803.m to exist, and there is no reasonable way for a
# Containerfile's own RUN steps to fetch+checksum-verify it during a build
# (network access during build is best avoided, and the real fetch script
# is meant to be run once per checkout, not baked into every image build).
# So this image bakes in whatever data/*.m is present on disk at build
# time -- run `uv run scripts/fetch_csiro_nem_data.py` on the host before
# `podman build` if data/ is empty. data/nemosis_cache/ (Lab 4's AEMO
# download cache, ~160MB, unrelated to Lab 3) is excluded below.
.venv/
.git/
logs/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
data/nemosis_cache/
# data/models/ holds GGUF model weight(s) for a concurrent llama.cpp/
# PowerMCP kube-manifest task in this same session (out of this
# Containerfile's scope, and multi-GB -- also observed mid-write during
# this build, which made an unfiltered `podman build` fail with
# "archive/tar: write too long"). Not needed by orchestrator.py --step
# sweep.
data/models/
